**Lemma 3.1 (rank locus and fixed range compression).** For $z=(u,v,w)\in
\mathbb C^3$ put $K(z)=uD+vT+wS$. Then

$$
K(z)=\begin{pmatrix}h_0u&av&cw\\bv&h_1u&0\\dw&0&h_2u\end{pmatrix},\qquad
\det K(z)=h_0h_1h_2\,u(u^2-\alpha v^2-\beta w^2).
\tag{CA.14}
$$

Every nonzero singular direction has rank exactly two. Its locus is the
whole plane $u=0$ together with the whole quadratic locus
$z^TB_0z=0$, where $B_0=\operatorname{diag}(1,-\alpha,-\beta)$.

Proof. Expanding the first row gives
$h_0h_1h_2u^3-abh_2uv^2-cdh_1uw^2$. For $u\ne0$, the minor in
rows/columns $1,2$ is $h_1h_2u^2\ne0$. For $u=0,z\ne0$, column $0$
is nonzero in coordinates $1,2$, and a nonzero column $1$ or $2$ lies in
coordinate $0$. They are independent and the other columns are parallel.
This gives rank two and excludes nonzero rank-one matrices in this span.
The equations use complex squares, not squared moduli.

For an actual encoder fix two independent columns: columns $1,2$ if
$u\ne0$; columns $0,1$ if $u=0,v\ne0$; columns $0,2$ otherwise. Denote
them $b_1,b_2$ and set

$$
q_1=b_1/\|b_1\|,\qquad
q_2=\frac{b_2-q_1(q_1^\dagger b_2)}
 {\|b_2-q_1(q_1^\dagger b_2)\|},\qquad U_z=(q_1,q_2).
\tag{CA.15}
$$

The independence just proved makes both denominators positive.
$U_z^\dagger U_z=I_2$ and $U_zU_z^\dagger K(z)=K(z)$. Thus the
encoder matrix $U_z^\dagger K(z)$ into dimension two and full TP live
decoder by $EU_z$ have composite $EK(z)$. The choices depend on fixed
coefficients, never on the input. Zero matrices are omitted. Joint
normalization, supplied in §6, makes these branches TNI. $\square$

